{"page": 1, "text": "Visible text of EX-99.1_2026-10-27_a20261027ex991pressrelease.htm, sha256 6df511b4d3dd8bdc9f5fecb50fbfa29aef45f45f8a0089c702f472a7b471d34d.\nEX-99.1 2 a20261027ex991pressrelease.htm EX-99.1\nExhibit 99.1 N E W S R E L E A S E\nContact: Investor Relations Inquiries Media Inquiries\nJennifer Gilligan Sara Garland\nSenior Vice President, Finance & Investor Relations Chief Communications Officer\n(212) 549-1306 (314) 445-0790\nFOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE\nCENTENE CORPORATION REPORTS THIRD QUARTER 2026 RESULTS -- Third Quarter GAAP Diluted Loss Per Share of $(0.14); Adjusted Diluted Earnings Per Share of $0.58 -- -- Increases 2026 GAAP Diluted EPS Guidance: Greater than $3.46 & Adjusted Diluted EPS Greater than $5.20 --\n\u2022Increases 2026 full year adjusted diluted EPS guidance by $0.40. \u2022Consolidated HBR of 92.7% in the third quarter, better than expectations, driven by the Medicare segment, with Medicaid and Marketplace on track. \u2022Full year 2026 HBR mid-point expectation improved by 15 basis points to 90.75%. \u2022Debt reduced by $1.1 billion since June 30, 2026, including full redemption of 2027 Senior Notes in October.\nST. LOUIS, October 27, 2026 -- Centene Corporation (NYSE: CNC) (the Company) announced today its financial results for the third quarter ended September 30, 2026. In summary, the 2026 third quarter results were as follows:\nTotal revenues (in millions) $ 50,647\nPremium and service revenues (in millions) $ 45,105\nHealth benefits ratio 92.7 %\nSG&A expense ratio 7.2 %\nAdjusted SG&A expense ratio (1) 6.5 %\nGAAP diluted loss per share $ (0.14)\nAdjusted diluted earnings per share (1) $ 0.58\nTotal cash flow (used in) operations (in millions) $ (3,669)\n(1) Represents a non-GAAP financial measure. A full reconciliation of the adjusted diluted earnings (loss) per share and adjusted selling, general and administrative (SG&A) expenses is shown in the Non-GAAP Financial Presentation section of this release.\n\"Solid underlying fundamentals within our core businesses have powered a faster recovery to our earnings trajectory than previously anticipated,\" said Chief Executive Officer of Centene, Sarah M. London. \"We are pleased with the progress our teams have made in delivering increased margin to power our mission of transforming the health of the communities we serve, one person at a time. We remain focused on a strong finish to 2026 and building on this progress in 2027.\" 1\nMembership\nThe following table sets forth membership by line of business:\nSeptember 30,\n2026 2025\nTraditional Medicaid (1) 10,544,300 11,115,400\nHigh Acuity Medicaid (2) 1,351,600 1,591,000\nTotal Medicaid 11,895,900 12,706,400\nMarketplace 3,403,300 5,828,100\nIndividual and Commercial Group (3) 497,400 447,900\nTotal Commercial 3,900,700 6,276,000\nMedicare (4) 954,400 1,013,200\nMedicare Prescription Drug Plan (PDP) 8,947,200 7,972,500\nTotal at-risk membership 25,698,200 27,968,100\n"}
{"page": 2, "text": "(1) Membership includes Temporary Assistance for Needy Families (TANF), Medicaid Expansion, Children's Health Insurance Program (CHIP), Foster Care, and Behavioral Health.\n(2) Membership includes Aged, Blind, or Disabled (ABD), Intellectual and Developmental Disabilities (IDD), Long-Term Services and Supports (LTSS), and Medicare-Medicaid Plans (MMP) Duals. The Company operated MMPs through December 31, 2025. In 2026 these members are included in Medicare as a result of the Centers for Medicare and Medicaid Services (CMS) transition to Dual Eligible Special Needs Plans (D-SNP) based integration.\n(3) Membership includes Commercial Group, CHOICE Arrangements (formerly Individual Coverage Health Reimbursement Arrangement, or ICHRA) and Other Off-Exchange Individual.\n(4) Membership includes Medicare Advantage, Medicare Supplement, and Applicable Integrated Plans (AIPs) as a result of the CMS transition to D-SNP based integration in 2026.\nPremium and Service Revenues\nThe following table sets forth supplemental revenue information ($ in millions):\nThree Months Ended September 30,\n2026 2025 % Change\nMedicaid $ 24,039 $ 23,171 4 %\nCommercial 8,700 10,992 (21) %\nMedicare (1) 11,263 9,391 20 %\nOther 1,103 1,344 (18) %\nTotal premium and service revenues $ 45,105 $ 44,898 0.5 %\n(1) Medicare includes Medicare Advantage, Medicare PDP and Medicare Supplement.\nStatement of Operations: Three Months Ended September 30, 2026\n\u2022For the third quarter of 2026, premium and service revenues increased 0.5% to $45.1 billion from $44.9 billion in the comparable period of 2025. The increase was primarily driven by premium yield and membership growth in the PDP business, rate increases in Marketplace and in the Medicaid business to address medical trend, Marketplace risk adjustment revenue transfer for the 2026 benefit year, and state directed payments. The increases were partially offset by lower Marketplace and Medicaid membership.\n\u2022Health benefits ratio (HBR) of 92.7% for the third quarter of 2026, unchanged from 92.7% in the comparable period in 2025. The consolidated HBR benefited from a lower Marketplace HBR resulting from improved pricing and risk transfer reflecting the acuity of the Marketplace membership as well as strong fundamental performance in both the Medicare Advantage and PDP businesses. The HBR in 2025 was positively impacted by a decrease to the premium deficiency reserve versus no premium deficiency reserve in 2026 for our Medicare Advantage business as a result of our progression towards profitability.\n2\n"}
{"page": 3, "text": "\u2022The SG&A expense ratio was 7.2% for the third quarter of 2026, compared to 7.0% in the third quarter of 2025. The adjusted SG&A expense ratio was 6.5% for the third quarter of 2026, compared to 7.0% in the third quarter of 2025. The increase in the SG&A expense ratio was primarily driven by enterprise optimization severance and vendor costs. The decrease in the adjusted SG&A expense ratio was driven by strong cost management, leveraging of expenses over higher revenues and reduced Marketplace membership, which operates at a meaningfully higher SG&A expense ratio. The decrease was also driven by growth in the PDP business, which operates at a meaningfully lower SG&A expense ratio as compared to the overall company.\n\u2022The effective tax rate was 46.7% for the third quarter of 2026, compared to 0.6% in the third quarter of 2025. For the third quarter of 2026, our effective tax rate on adjusted earnings was 14.5%, compared to 2.5% in the third quarter of 2025. The GAAP and adjusted effective tax rates for 2026 reflect a decrease to the estimated annual effective tax rate applied to year-to-date operating results. The GAAP and adjusted effective tax rates for 2025 reflect the impact of estimating interim period taxes on the year-to-date tax method. The effective tax rate for 2025 also reflects the non-deductible nature of the goodwill impairment.\n\u2022GAAP diluted loss per share of $(0.14) for the third quarter of 2026.\n\u2022Adjusted diluted earnings per share (EPS) of $0.58 for the third quarter of 2026.\n\u2022Cash flow used in operations for the third quarter of 2026 was $3.7 billion, primarily driven by the timing of pass through, premium and other payments, as expected.\nBalance Sheet\nAt September 30, 2026, the Company had cash, investments and restricted deposits of $39.9 billion and maintained $175 million of cash available for general corporate use. Medical claims liabilities totaled $21.5 billion. The Company's days in claims payable (DCP) was 48 days, an increase of one day as compared to the second quarter of 2026.\nDuring the third quarter of 2026, the Company repurchased $558 million of the Company's par value senior notes due 2027 and 2028. Following the senior note repurchase, total debt was $15.5 billion, which included no borrowings on the $4.0 billion Revolving Credit Facility at quarter end. In October 2026, the debt repurchase program was increased by $2.0 billion and subsequently the Company repurchased the remaining $569 million of its par value Senior Notes due 2027. With the increase and subsequent repurchase, there was $1.9 billion available under the senior note debt repurchase program as of October 27, 2026.\nOutlook\nPlease refer to the Forward-Looking Statements, which should be reviewed in conjunction with the Company's 2026 outlook.\n"}
{"page": 4, "text": "The Company is updating its 2026 GAAP diluted EPS guidance floor to greater than $3.46 and its 2026 adjusted diluted EPS guidance floor to greater than $5.20. Additionally, the Company is decreasing its HBR guidance range to 90.4% to 91.1% and its interest expense guidance range to $600 million to $620 million. 3\nThe Company's annual guidance for 2026 is as follows and will be discussed further on our conference call:\nFull Year 2026\nGAAP diluted EPS > $3.46\nAdjusted diluted EPS (1) > $5.20\n(1) A full reconciliation of adjusted diluted EPS is shown in the Non-GAAP Financial Presentation section of this release.\nFull Year 2026\nLow High\nTotal revenues (in billions) $ 196.5 $ 200.5\nPremium and service revenues (in billions) $ 173.0 $ 177.0\nHBR 90.4 % 91.1 %\nSG&A expense ratio 7.2 % 7.8 %\nAdjusted SG&A expense ratio (2) 6.9 % 7.5 %\nEffective tax rate 26.5 % 27.5 %\nAdjusted effective tax rate (3) 25.5 % 26.5 %\nDiluted shares outstanding (in millions) 497.0 500.0\n(2) Adjusted SG&A expense ratio excludes severance costs due to enterprise optimization and contract exits of approximately $355 million to $405 million, enterprise optimization third-party vendor costs of approximately $85 million to $115 million and acquisition and divestiture related expenses of approximately $1 million.\n(3) Adjusted effective tax rate excludes income tax effects of adjustments of approximately $266 million to $270 million.\nConference Call\nAs previously announced, the Company will host a conference call Tuesday, October 27, 2026, at 8:30 a.m. ET to review the financial results for the third quarter ended September 30, 2026.\nInvestors and other interested parties are invited to listen to the conference call by dialing 1-877-883-0383 (toll free) in the U.S. and Canada; +1-412-902-6506 (toll) from abroad, including the following Elite Entry Number: 1565730 to expedite caller registration; or via a live, audio webcast on the Company's website at www.centene.com, under the Investors section.\nA webcast replay will be available for on-demand listening shortly following the completion of the call for the next 12 months or until 11:59 p.m. ET on Tuesday, October 26, 2027, at the aforementioned URL. In addition, a digital audio playback will be available until 9 a.m. ET on Tuesday, November 3, 2026, by dialing 1-855-669-9658 (toll free) in North America, or +1-412-317-0088 (toll) from abroad, and entering access code 581422.\nNon-GAAP Financial Presentation\n"}
